Local conjugacy in prosolvable groups — Lean development
Prepared for M.C.B. with AI assistance from OpenAI Codex.

This project directly adapts lcp-formalized; its source fingerprints are in
reports/reused-lcp-sources.json. That project in turn adapts the development in
local-conjugacy-prosolvable-formalized. Its source-file fingerprints are
recorded in reports/reused-sources.json. The current manuscript snapshot is
identified in reports/source-fingerprints.json.

The original mathematical manuscript and cited literature retain their own
copyright and licenses; this repository's Apache-2.0 license covers the new
formalization code and documentation, not those cited works.

The Apache-2.0 license text and metadata validator were taken from
PalomarRegistry/PalomarTemplate, commit
d06eea17a234d0936798a78fa23f8a69e80374a7 (Apache-2.0).
The bundled-Comparator workflow follows the PalomarTemplate instructions
at https://github.com/PalomarRegistry/PalomarTemplate/blob/main/scripts/verify-comparator.sh
as rechecked on 2026-09-30.

QuotientReduction.lean adapts an earlier local Lean file,
_local_conjugacy_inclusion.lean, found in the user's prove2me_workspace.
Its fingerprint is recorded in reports/source-fingerprints.json. It supplies
only an algebraic reduction, not a proof of the manuscript's full corollary.

Mathlib and its dependencies retain their respective licenses and authorship.

The productEquiv construction in LocalConjugacy/NilpotentCoefficients.lean
